msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# AutoTuner Example\n"
"\n"
"This example demonstrates how to use the AutoTuner to automatically search for optimal hyperparameters. The AutoTuner can automatically adjust model hyperparameters based on the provided search space to achieve the best performance.\n"
"\n"
"## Features\n"
"\n"
"- Supports multiple search strategies (grid search, random search, Bayesian optimization)\n"
"- Provides rich hyperparameter search space definitions\n"
"- Supports parallel search to improve efficiency\n"
"- Provides detailed search process logging and result visualization\n"
"\n"
"## Quick Start\n"
"\n"
"### 1. Define the Search Space\n"
"\n"
"First, define the hyperparameter search space you want to explore:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"from autotuner import SearchSpace, Hyperparameter\n"
"\n"
"# Define the search space\n"
"search_space = SearchSpace([\n"
"    Hyperparameter(\"learning_rate\", 0.001, 0.1, log_scale=True),\n"
"    Hyperparameter(\"batch_size\", [16, 32, 64, 128]),\n"
"    Hyperparameter(\"num_layers\", 1, 5, step=1),\n"
"    Hyperparameter(\"activation\", [\"relu\", \"tanh\", \"sigmoid\"])\n"
"])\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 2. Define the Objective Function\n"
"\n"
"Define the objective function to be optimized. This function receives a set of hyperparameters and returns a score to be optimized (higher is better):\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"def objective(params):\n"
"    # Train the model using the given hyperparameters\n"
"    model = create_model(\n"
"        learning_rate=params[\"learning_rate\"],\n"
"        batch_size=params[\"batch_size\"],\n"
"        num_layers=params[\"num_layers\"],\n"
"        activation=params[\"activation\"]\n"
"    )\n"
"    \n"
"    # Train and evaluate\n"
"    accuracy = train_and_evaluate(model)\n"
"    \n"
"    return accuracy\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 3. Run AutoTuner\n"
"\n"
"Use the AutoTuner to search for the optimal hyperparameters:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"from autotuner import AutoTuner\n"
"\n"
"# Create AutoTuner instance\n"
"tuner = AutoTuner(\n"
"    search_space=search_space,\n"
"    objective=objective,\n"
"    strategy=\"bayesian\",  # Options: \"grid\", \"random\", \"bayesian\"\n"
"    max_trials=100,\n"
"    n_jobs=4  # Number of parallel workers\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"# Start searching\n"
"best_params, best_score = tuner.optimize()\n"
"\n"
"print(f\"Best hyperparameters: {best_params}\")\n"
"print(f\"Best score: {best_score}\")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Advanced Usage\n"
"\n"
"### Custom Search Strategy\n"
"\n"
"You can customize the search strategy by inheriting the base class:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"from autotuner import BaseStrategy\n"
"\n"
"class CustomStrategy(BaseStrategy):\n"
"    def suggest(self, history):\n"
"        # Implement your own suggestion logic\n"
"        return suggested_params\n"
"    \n"
"    def update(self, params, score):\n"
"        # Update internal state\n"
"        pass\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### Early Stopping\n"
"\n"
"Set early stopping conditions to save resources:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"tuner = AutoTuner(\n"
"    search_space=search_space,\n"
"    objective=objective,\n"
"    strategy=\"bayesian\",\n"
"    max_trials=100,\n"
"    early_stopping={\n"
"        \"patience\": 10,  # Stop if no improvement after 10 trials\n"
"        \"min_delta\": 0.001  # Minimum improvement threshold\n"
"    }\n"
")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### Result Visualization\n"
"\n"
"Visualize the search process and results:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"from autotuner import visualize\n"
"\n"
"# Plot the search process\n"
"visualize.plot_search_history(tuner.history)\n"
"\n"
"# Plot the importance of hyperparameters\n"
"visualize.plot_hyperparameter_importance(tuner.history)\n"
"\n"
"# Plot the optimization landscape\n"
"visualize.plot_optimization_landscape(tuner.history)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Notes\n"
"\n"
"1. The objective function should be deterministic as much as possible; otherwise, the search results may be unstable.\n"
"2. For large-scale searches, it is recommended to use the Bayesian optimization strategy to improve efficiency.\n"
"3. The search space should be defined reasonably based on the actual problem to avoid unnecessary waste of resources.\n"
"4. During parallel search, ensure that the objective function is thread-safe.\n"

msgid "自动调优 （Autotune）"
msgstr "Autotune"

msgid "如果你希望先了解 Triton-Ascend autotune 的推荐用法、`configs=[]` 的含义，以及自动 Tiling 的适用边界，建议先阅读 [Triton-Ascend autotune 使用指南](../autotune_guide.md)。"
msgstr "If you want to first understand the recommended usage of Triton-Ascend autotune, the meaning of `configs=[]`, and the applicable boundaries of automatic Tiling, it is recommended to first read the [Triton-Ascend autotune usage guide](../autotune_guide.md)."

msgid "在本节中，我们将展示使用 Triton 的 autotune 方法自动选择最优的 kernel 配置参数。当前 Triton-Ascend autotune 完全兼容社区 autotune 的使用方法（参考[社区文档](https://triton-lang.org/main/python-api/generated/triton.autotune.html)），即需要用户手动传入一些定义好的 triton.Config，然后 autotune 会通过 benchmark 的方式选择其中的最优 kernel 配置；此外 Triton-Ascend 提供了**进阶的 autotune** 用法，用户无需提供triton kernel 的切分轴、tiling 轴等信息，autotune 会根据triton kernel语义自动解析切分轴、tiling轴等信息，并自动生成一些可能最优的 kernel 配置，然后通过 benchmark 或者 profiling 的方式选择其中的最优配置。"
msgstr "In this section, we will demonstrate how to use Triton's autotune method to automatically select the optimal kernel configuration parameters. The current Triton-Ascend autotune is fully compatible with the community autotune usage (refer to the [community documentation](https://triton-lang.org/main/python-api/generated/triton.autotune.html)), which requires users to manually pass in a set of predefined triton.Config objects, and then autotune selects the optimal kernel configuration among them through benchmarking. In addition, Triton-Ascend provides an **advanced autotune** usage where users do not need to provide information such as the split axes or tiling axes of the Triton kernel. The autotune automatically parses the split axes, tiling axes, and other information based on the Triton kernel semantics, automatically generates a set of potentially optimal kernel configurations, and then selects the optimal configuration through benchmarking or profiling."

msgid "说明： 当前Triton-Ascend autotune支持block size、multibuffer（编译器的优化），因为硬件架构差异不支持num_warps、num_stages参数，未来还会持续增加autotune可调项。"
msgstr "Note: Currently, Triton-Ascend autotune supports block size and multibuffer (compiler optimizations). Due to hardware architecture differences, the num_warps and num_stages parameters are not supported. More autotune tunable options will be added in the future."

msgid "社区 autotune 使用示例"
msgstr "Community autotune usage example"

msgid "import torch, torch_npu\\n"
msgstr "import torch, torch_npu"

msgid "进阶 autotune 使用示例"
msgstr "Advanced autotune usage example"

msgid "# The following explains the key parameter usage differences between the advanced autotune and the community version\\n"
msgstr "# The following explains the key parameter usage differences between the advanced autotune and the community version"

msgid "说明："
msgstr "Explanation:"

msgid "Triton-Ascend默认采取benchmark的方式取片上计算时间，当设置环境变量`export TRITON_BENCH_METHOD=\"npu\"`后，会通过`torch_npu.profiler.profile`的方式获取每个kernel配置下的片上计算时间，对于一些triton kernel计算快速的情况，例如小shape算子，相较于默认方式能够获取更准确的计算时间，但是会显著增加整体autotune的时间，请谨慎开启"
msgstr "Triton-Ascend defaults to using the benchmark method to obtain on-chip computation time. When the environment variable `export TRITON_BENCH_METHOD=\"npu\"` is set, the on-chip computation time for each kernel configuration is obtained via `torch_npu.profiler.profile`. For some triton kernels that compute quickly, such as small-shape operators, this can yield more accurate computation time compared to the default method, but it will significantly increase the overall autotune time. Please enable it with caution."

msgid "目前该进阶用法针对的是 Vector 类算子，不支持 Cube 类算子。更多进阶使用示例可以参考[autotune进阶使用示例](https://gitcode.com/Ascend/triton-ascend/tree/main/third_party/ascend/unittest/autotune_ut/)。"
msgstr "Currently, this advanced usage is targeted at Vector-type operators and does not support Cube-type operators. For more advanced usage examples, please refer to the [autotune advanced usage examples](https://gitcode.com/Ascend/triton-ascend/tree/main/third_party/ascend/unittest/autotune_ut/)."

msgid "参数自动解析"
msgstr "Automatic parameter parsing"

msgid "执行参数自动解析前首先会获取`kernel`函数调用时未传入的参数，**将未传入的参数作为切分轴和分块轴参数的候选项**。"
msgstr "Before executing automatic parameter parsing, the function first retrieves the parameters not passed during the `kernel` function call, **using the unpassed parameters as candidates for the split axis and block axis parameters**."

msgid "@triton.jit\\n"
msgstr "@triton.jit"

msgid "切分轴参数解析"
msgstr "Parsing of split axis parameters."

msgid "切分轴参数解析依据 `tl.program_id()`分核语句来确定 ，系统通过分析程序中 `tl.program_id()` 变量的使用情况及其与其他变量的乘法运算识别潜在的切分轴参数（当前支持直接相乘或通过中间变量间接相乘的场景），并根据候选参数列表（用户未提供的参数）进行过滤。"
msgstr "The axis split parameter parsing is determined based on the `tl.program_id()` core division statement. The system identifies potential axis split parameters by analyzing the usage of the `tl.program_id()` variable in the program and its multiplication operations with other variables (currently supporting scenarios of direct multiplication or indirect multiplication through intermediate variables), and filters them according to the candidate parameter list (parameters not provided by the user)."

msgid "最后通过掩码比较和 `autotune` 中传入的 `key` 确认当前参数对应的切分轴。"
msgstr "Finally, confirm the split axis corresponding to the current parameters through mask comparison and the `key` passed into `autotune`."

msgid "注意：1. 分割轴参数必须要与 `tl.program_id()` 相乘。 2. 必须要进行掩码比较，且该轴对应的key需要直接作为右值或以key为参数的min函数作为右值，才能对应到具体的切分轴，否则会导致参数解析失败。3. 识别出的分割轴参数仅限于候选参数列表，确保只有那些可以通过自动调优动态调整的参数才会被考虑。"
msgstr "Note: 1. The split axis parameter must be multiplied by `tl.program_id()`. 2. A mask comparison must be performed, and the key corresponding to that axis needs to be used directly as the right-hand value or as the right-hand value of a min function with the key as its parameter, in order to map to the specific split axis; otherwise, parameter parsing will fail. 3. The recognized split axis parameters are limited to the candidate parameter list, ensuring that only those parameters that can be dynamically adjusted through auto-tuning are considered."

msgid "@triton.autotune(\\n"
msgstr "@triton.autotune("

msgid "分块轴参数解析"
msgstr "Block axis parameter parsing"

msgid "分块轴参数依据 `tl.arange()` ，`tl.range()`，`range()` 分块语句来确定。通过分析程序中`for` 循环里的 `tl.range()`，`tl.arange()`以及`range()` 的使用情况及其计算得到的变量来识别潜在的分块轴参数，提取 `tl.range()` 或 `range()` 中和 `tl.arange()` 的共同参数，并根据候选参数列表（用户未提供的参数）进行过滤。"
msgstr "Block axis parameters are determined based on the `tl.arange()`, `tl.range()`, and `range()` blocking statements. By analyzing the usage of `tl.range()`, `tl.arange()`, and `range()` in the `for` loops of the program, as well as the variables they compute, potential block axis parameters are identified. Common parameters between `tl.range()` or `range()` and `tl.arange()` are extracted and filtered according to the candidate parameter list (parameters not provided by the user)."

msgid "最后通过掩码比较和 `autotune` 中传入的 `key` 确认当前参数对应的分块轴。"
msgstr "Finally, through mask comparison and the `key` passed into `autotune`, the chunking axis corresponding to the current parameters is confirmed."

msgid "注意：1. 分块轴参数必须出现在 `tl.arange()` 的调用中，并且需在 `for` 循环中通过 `tl.range()`、`range()` 或整除运算（`//`）参与循环范围的计算。 2. 必须要进行掩码比较，且该轴对应的key需要直接作为右值或以key为参数的min函数作为右值，才能对应到具体的分块轴，否则会导致参数解析失败。3. 识别出的分块轴参数仅限于候选参数列表，确保只有那些可以通过自动调优动态调整的参数才会被考虑。"
msgstr "Note: 1. The block axis parameter must appear in the call to `tl.arange()` and must participate in the calculation of the loop range within the `for` loop via `tl.range()`, `range()`, or integer division (`//`). 2. A mask comparison must be performed, and the key corresponding to that axis must be used directly as the right-hand value or as the right-hand value of a min function with the key as its parameter, in order to map to the specific block axis; otherwise, parameter parsing will fail. 3. The identified block axis parameters are limited to the candidate parameter list, ensuring that only those parameters that can be dynamically adjusted through autotuning are considered."

msgid "低维轴参数解析"
msgstr "Low-dimensional axis parameter analysis"

msgid "低维轴参数解析依据 `tl.arange()` 分块语句来确定，通过分析程序中 `tl.arange()` 的使用情况及其计算得到的变量来识别潜在的低维轴参数，提取 `tl.arange()` 本身以及它参与计算的变量，通过是否进行切片操作来进行增维，以及通过判断增维维度来进行过滤。"
msgstr "Low-dimensional axis parameter analysis is determined based on the `tl.arange()` chunking statements. By analyzing the usage of `tl.arange()` in the program and the variables it computes, potential low-dimensional axis parameters are identified. The `tl.arange()` itself and the variables it participates in computing are extracted, dimension augmentation is performed based on whether slicing operations are applied, and filtering is carried out by determining the augmented dimensions."

msgid "最后通过掩码比较和 `autotune` 中传入的 `key` 确认当前kernel的低维轴。"
msgstr "Finally, confirm the low-dimensional axis of the current kernel through mask comparison and the `key` passed in `autotune`."

msgid "注意：1. 低维轴必须要通过`tl.arange()`进行计算，并进行切片。并在非最低维进行维度扩充或不参与切片，才会被识别。 2. 若不进行掩码比较则无法对应到具体的低维轴，会导致参数解析失败。"
msgstr "Note: 1. The low-dimensional axis must be computed via `tl.arange()` and sliced. It will only be recognized if dimension expansion is performed on non-lowest dimensions or it does not participate in slicing. 2. Without mask comparison, it cannot correspond to a specific low-dimensional axis, which will cause parameter parsing to fail."

msgid "参数指针解析"
msgstr "Parameter pointer resolution"

msgid "指针类型的参数解析依据该参数是否参与 `tl.load()` 和 `tl.store()` 的访存类语句来确定。"
msgstr "Pointer-type parameter parsing is determined based on whether the parameter participates in memory-access statements such as `tl.load()` and `tl.store()`."

msgid "首先解析出kernel函数中的所有参数，之后递归寻找每一个参数参与计算的所有变量。"
msgstr "First, parse out all parameters in the kernel function, then recursively find all variables that each parameter participates in for computation."

msgid "如果该参数直接参与或该参数计算得到的中间变量间接参与 `tl.load()` 和 `tl.store()` 的第一个参数计算，则认为该参数是一个指针类型参数。"
msgstr "If the parameter directly participates in or the intermediate variable calculated from the parameter indirectly participates in the computation of the first argument of `tl.load()` and `tl.store()`, the parameter is considered a pointer-type parameter."

msgid "注意：1. 使用 `tl.constexpr` 修饰的变量不会是指针类型的变量，不进行后续解析 2. 只计算参数直接参与或参数经过一次计算得到的中间变量间接参与的访存类语句，若参数进行两次以上计算得到的中间变量不进行统计。"
msgstr "Note: 1. Variables modified by `tl.constexpr` will not be pointer-type variables and will not undergo subsequent parsing. 2. Only memory-access statements where the parameter directly participates or where an intermediate variable obtained through one calculation of the parameter indirectly participates are counted; intermediate variables obtained through two or more calculations of the parameter are not included in the statistics."

msgid "@triton.autotune(...)\\n"
msgstr "@triton.autotune(...)"

msgid "更多功能"
msgstr "More features"

msgid "自动生成最优配置的 Profiling 结果"
msgstr "Profiling results for automatically generating optimal configuration."

msgid "# Automatically generate profiling results of the current optimal autotune kernel configuration in the `auto_profile_dir` directory, i.e., performance data collected via `torch_npu.profiler.profile`\\n"
msgstr "# Automatically generate profiling results of the current optimal autotune kernel configuration in the `auto_profile_dir` directory, i.e., performance data collected via `torch_npu.profiler.profile`"
